      "message": "Reading through `charge_manager_force_ceil()`, it calls through to `board_set_charge_limit()`, and it appears that most boards will set their input current limit to `MAX(charge_ma, CONFIG_CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT)`, with many (but not all) boards setting `CONFIG_CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT` to 512 mA.  \n\nAm I mis-reading this, or will this cause most boards to essentially use 500mA despite this logic to lower the current?",
