      "writtenOn": "2022-10-24T22:41:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "b/243189930 (https://crrev.com/c/3905355) discusses that some. I think `CONFIG_CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT` is badly defined and boards that use it as a minimum current should be fixed: that should be the non-PD current limit only, as currently configured by charger drivers.\nBoards should not use it as a minimum charge current, though there might be a tricky interaction between pSnkStdby limits and low-battery situtations (which aren\u0027t currently handled well right now either, since we can have the same problem if we overcurrent the source and cause it to shut down).\n\nIn any case, that seems like something to address after this CL.",
